#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:11
msgid "First steps with ROS - learning path"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:14
msgid ""
"ROS provides the framework, tools, and libraries for building robotic "
"applications. This learning path introduces installation, Turtlesim, core "
"communication concepts, introspection, launch files, and data playback. "
"After completing it, you will be ready to start working with ROS client "
"libraries and tutorials."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:24
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:27
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:29
msgid ""
"The ROS framework is the “plumbing” which makes communication between "
"different parts of a robot possible. It includes messaging, standard "
"interfaces, and support for multiple programming languages and platforms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:32
msgid ""
"You need to understand the fundamental concepts of the framework before you "
"can work with ROS to develop or maintain applications. The Turtlesim tool "
"and the tutorials in this site will help you get up to speed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:37
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:39
msgid ""
"None. The steps outlined in this article will guide you through downloading "
"and installing everything you need to learn the basics of ROS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:43
msgid "Steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:46
msgid "1 Learn about fundamental concepts behind ROS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:48
msgid ":doc:`About ROS <About-ROS>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:49
msgid ":doc:`ROS-Framework/About-Nodes`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:50
msgid ":doc:`ROS-Framework/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:51
msgid ":doc:`ROS-Framework/About-Parameters`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:54
msgid "2 Install ROS and Turtlesim"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:56
msgid ""
"ROS installation includes the essential packages for working with ROS. If "
"you're familiar with Linux, our recommended platform is Ubuntu (deb "
"packages). Otherwise, a good alternative installation platform is Windows "
"(binaries): :doc:`Installation options <Get-Started/Installation>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:60
msgid ""
"After installing ROS, set up your environment so that ROS commands, "
"packages, and workspaces are available in each new shell: :doc:`Set up your "
"environment <Get-Started/Configuring-ROS2-Environment>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:62
msgid ""
"With Turtlesim, a lightweight 2D simulation tool designed for beginners, you "
"can learn core ROS concepts in a simple visual environment: :doc:`Set up "
"Turtlesim <Get-Started/Introducing-Turtlesim/Introducing-Turtlesim>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:65
msgid ""
"3 Try out working with the main communication components of the ROS framework"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:67
msgid ""
"Use Turtlesim to familiarize yourself with the main communication components "
"and try out messaging in the ROS framework."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:69
msgid ""
"Complete the nodes tutorial: :doc:`ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/"
"Understanding-ROS2-Nodes/Understanding-ROS2-Nodes`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:70
msgid ""
"Complete the topics tutorial: :doc:`ROS-Framework/interfaces/topics/"
"Understanding-ROS2-Topics/Understanding-ROS2-Topics`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:71
msgid ""
"Complete the services tutorial: :doc:`ROS-Framework/interfaces/services/"
"Working-with-services/Understanding-ROS2-Services/Understanding-ROS2-"
"Services`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:72
msgid ""
"Complete the parameters tutorial: :doc:`ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-"
"with-parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters/Understanding-ROS2-Parameters`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:73
msgid ""
"Complete the actions tutorial: :doc:`ROS-Framework/interfaces/actions/"
"Working-with-actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions/Understanding-ROS2-Actions`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:76
msgid "4 Learn about introspection with logs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:78
msgid ""
"Introspection enables you to see information about how a system is "
"operating. Nodes use logs to output messages concerning events and status in "
"a variety of ways."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:81
msgid ""
"To see introspection through logs in action, complete the CLI logging "
"tutorial: [coming soon]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:84
msgid "5 Learn about using launch files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:86
msgid ""
"Launch files allow you to start and configure a number of processes "
"containing ROS nodes simultaneously, instead of opening multiple terminals "
"and re-entering configuration details for each node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:88
msgid ""
"Complete the launch files tutorial: :doc:`ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-"
"nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes/Launching-Multiple-Nodes`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:91
msgid "6 Learn about data recording and playback"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:93
msgid ""
"Sometimes it's useful to replay data to reproduce the results of your tests "
"and experiments, to debug your robot's behaviour, or to share your work with "
"others."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:95
msgid ""
"Complete the recording and playback tutorial: :doc:`ROS-Framework/interfaces/"
"Working-with-interfaces/Recording-And-Playing-Back-Data/Recording-And-"
"Playing-Back-Data`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:98
msgid "7 Learn about data visualization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:100
msgid ""
"RViz lets you inspect 3D data from a running ROS system, such as shapes, "
"sensor data, and robot models."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:102
msgid ""
"Complete the data visualization tutorial: :doc:`Developer-Tools/"
"Visualization/RViz/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes/Marker-Sending-Basic-Shapes`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:105
msgid "Next steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/First-Steps.rst:107
msgid ""
"The tutorials in this learning path use the ROS command-line interface (CLI) "
"to introduce the core ROS concepts and show you how to interact with them. "
"To build your own ROS components, such as nodes written in C++ or Python, "
"you use the ROS client library APIs. We recommend getting comfortable with "
"the CLI first, then familiarizing yourself with ROS client "
"libraries: :doc:`ROS-Framework/About-Client-Libraries`"
msgstr ""
